<title>SWEDEN: Electrolux jumps on restructuring plan.</title>
<headline>Electrolux jumps on restructuring plan.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish appliance maker Electrolux shares jumped in Thursday afternoon trade on news of a 2.5 billion crown restructuring programme.</p>
<p>At 1230 GMT Electrolux shares were 15 crowns higher at 480, rising from trading five crowns under Wednesday's closing levels.</p>
<p>Electrolux, headed by new managing director Michael Treschow, said it would close about 25 plants and cut 12,000 staff over the next two years.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a positive reaction in the market place but it was not a total surprise,&quot; one Stockholm based analyst said. &quot;They needed to do something about their profitabilty and that was what Mr Treschow was brought in to do.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
